id: pm-gh1549
title: "GH-1549: fence item commits after an expired mutation lease is taken over"
description: "A newly received GitHub report demonstrates a stale SDK mutateItem callback silently overwriting a newer committed CLI update after TTL takeover. Independently reproduced through the public SDK entrypoint on current744a4c95a in a disposable non-Git tracker, with only locks.ttl_seconds changed to1. The peer commits successfully, the stale SDK writer is not refused, and the final title is Stale overwrite. This is small-N correctness, separate from large-N lock throughput and checkpoint claim-generation fencing."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[4]: bug,concurrency,data-integrity,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-22T14:40:08.187Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-22T14:40:08.187Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Deterministic cross-process and same-process controls preserve a newer write after lease takeover; Stale commits return a typed conflict with bounded ownership/generation evidence and no item/history write; Preserve dead-owner recovery and explicit stale-lock policy without unsafe force advice; Audit other SDK mutation paths and document the lease/fencing contract
parent: pm-dj98
risk: high
confidence: high
severity: high
expected_result: "After another writer takes over and commits, the stale mutation refuses before overwriting item or authoritative history state; the newer committed value remains unchanged. Preserve supported stale takeover and proven-dead-owner recovery policies."
actual_result: "Isolated public-SDK plus CLI reproduction: ttl1, newerCommitted=true, staleWriterRefused=false, finalTitle=Stale overwrite. Current source remains affected; no production tracker was used or modified."
